# pgs.sh _redirects (Netlify syntax). First match wins, so specific rules precede
# the catch-all.
#
# The in-wiki blog/ section was the first implementation and was removed once the
# Hugo blog superseded it; its two posts were near-verbatim duplicates of published
# posts. These 301s send the old URLs to the canonical copies instead of 404ing.
#
# NOTE: deliberately no `/*` catch-all here. wiki.infernalcode.com and
# volnixos-wiki.pgs.sh serve the SAME pgs project, so a blanket redirect to the
# custom domain would fire on the custom domain too and loop forever. The old
# hostname is handled by rel=canonical instead, which every page already emits.

/blog/why-mcp-servers-need-isolation/        https://infernalcode.com/posts/why-mcp-servers-need-isolation/          301
/blog/the-impermanence-bind-mount-symlink-trap/  https://infernalcode.com/posts/the-impermanence-bind-mount-symlink-trap/  301

# Blog index, archive, category and tag pages the plugin used to generate.
/blog/*                                      https://infernalcode.com/                                                301
